{# The light / dark switch of a page with no account: a share link, a public
   reading, a document sent to a customer. The suite has it in the account
   menu and the sign-in page in its corner; a guest had no way to change it.

   Driven by the `theme` entry (assets/theme.js), which every such page loads
   already: it finds the button by its id, shows the icon of the theme it
   would switch to and keeps the name in step. The labels travel with the
   button so the script has nothing to translate. Same frame as the suite's
   icon buttons (38 px), so it sits in a header next to them. #}
<button
    type="button"
    id="theme-toggle"
    class="inline-flex h-[38px] w-[38px] shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-line text-muted transition-colors hover:bg-surface-2 hover:text-primary focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-accent print:hidden {{ class ?? '' }}"
    data-label-light="{{ 'suite.nav.light_mode'|trans }}"
    data-label-dark="{{ 'suite.nav.dark_mode'|trans }}"
    aria-label="{{ 'suite.nav.dark_mode'|trans }}"
    title="{{ 'suite.nav.dark_mode'|trans }}"
>
    {{ include('@Shared/components/icon.html.twig', {name: 'moon', class: 'icon-moon w-5 h-5'}) }}
    {{ include('@Shared/components/icon.html.twig', {name: 'sun', class: 'icon-sun w-5 h-5'}) }}
</button>
